1
00:01:40,921 --> 00:01:41,546
Fuck!

2
00:01:44,063 --> 00:01:46,503
Foul! Are you blind?

3
00:01:46,504 --> 00:01:49,112
Shut up, put on your mask.
Hurry up!

4
00:01:55,671 --> 00:01:57,463
Yellow card next time.

5
00:02:02,046 --> 00:02:03,421
First position, en garde.

6
00:02:06,546 --> 00:02:07,546
Go!

7
00:02:11,754 --> 00:02:13,838
- Penalty!
- I was on the line!

8
00:02:13,968 --> 00:02:15,551
- First position.
- Bullshit!

9
00:02:15,655 --> 00:02:16,738
That's enough.

10
00:02:19,471 --> 00:02:20,346
Go!

11
00:02:26,421 --> 00:02:27,213
Damn!

12
00:02:31,713 --> 00:02:34,004
- He's out of bounds!
- Stop whining.

13
00:02:34,629 --> 00:02:37,588
First position.
I won't tell you again, hear?

14
00:02:45,654 --> 00:02:46,131
Okay.

15
00:02:47,704 --> 00:02:48,745
Go!

16
00:03:09,529 --> 00:03:11,987
Leïla Lakti, you're disqualified!

17
00:03:26,004 --> 00:03:27,504
I know. Don't bother.

18
00:03:29,302 --> 00:03:30,645
You just ruined your season.

19
00:03:30,646 --> 00:03:34,045
There was a foul, wasn't there?
He deserved it.

20
00:03:34,046 --> 00:03:35,332
But it's the ref's call.

21
00:03:35,499 --> 00:03:37,499
Stop, enough!
Okay, I got it!

22
00:03:44,771 --> 00:03:46,146
Nothing to say, Fanny?

23
00:03:46,813 --> 00:03:48,771
You let your emotions
control you.

24
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:51,521
Like your mother.

25
00:03:51,938 --> 00:03:55,104
- Was it a foul or not?
- That's not the point!

26
00:03:55,479 --> 00:03:56,896
Contain yourself.

27
00:03:57,479 --> 00:03:59,563
Get going, see you later.

28
00:04:05,229 --> 00:04:06,688
Can I drive?

29
00:04:07,896 --> 00:04:09,146
Please.

30
00:04:14,021 --> 00:04:14,979
Thanks.

31
00:04:15,146 --> 00:04:17,229
You asked so kindly.

32
00:04:27,854 --> 00:04:29,438
Ludo's your beau?

33
00:04:31,361 --> 00:04:33,945
Who says "beau" besides you?

34
00:04:34,758 --> 00:04:35,172
No .

35
00:04:36,938 --> 00:04:39,354
- Don't change the subject.
- No subject.

36
00:04:40,688 --> 00:04:42,729
- Are you in love?
- Come on...

37
00:04:44,896 --> 00:04:48,021
What about your date the other night?
How was it?

38
00:04:49,146 --> 00:04:51,229
I'm not in love, far from it.

39
00:04:51,729 --> 00:04:52,563
Yeah?

40
00:04:52,729 --> 00:04:54,938
I answered. Your turn.

41
00:04:55,313 --> 00:04:56,646
You're very nosy.

42
00:04:56,813 --> 00:05:00,063
No, I'm your mother.
Asking questions is normal.

43
00:05:02,563 --> 00:05:03,896
In a situationship?

44
00:05:05,688 --> 00:05:06,771
Yeah, you got it.

45
00:05:07,438 --> 00:05:08,271
Watch out!

46
00:05:40,979 --> 00:05:42,104
Mom!

47
00:05:42,688 --> 00:05:43,854
Mom!

48
00:05:53,938 --> 00:05:55,313
Sir!

49
00:05:57,521 --> 00:05:59,271
Sir, please!

50
00:06:00,646 --> 00:06:02,271
Please help!

51
00:06:03,104 --> 00:06:04,771
Wait!

52
00:06:10,313 --> 00:06:11,354
Mom!

53
00:07:50,271 --> 00:07:51,396
Hey.

54
00:07:52,688 --> 00:07:53,854
Hey.

55
00:08:56,396 --> 00:08:57,646
- Evening.
- Julien...

56
00:08:59,021 --> 00:09:00,813
Say bye.
Your Dad's waiting.

57
00:09:05,104 --> 00:09:06,229
<i>You guys good?</i>

58
00:09:07,146 --> 00:09:08,271
Where's the dope?

59
00:09:09,146 --> 00:09:10,313
20 kilos in all.

60
00:09:13,396 --> 00:09:14,146
Wanna play?

61
00:09:15,438 --> 00:09:16,438
Get lost.

62
00:09:50,271 --> 00:09:51,896
- Get in.
- Yes, sir.

63
00:09:58,188 --> 00:09:59,354
<i>It's Fanny.</i>

64
00:09:59,771 --> 00:10:01,604
<i>It's about Sofia.</i>

65
00:10:02,063 --> 00:10:03,729
<i>She had an accident.</i>

66
00:10:03,979 --> 00:10:05,771
<i>Call me back fast. Love ya.</i>

67
00:10:17,479 --> 00:10:22,938
THE ORPHANS

68
00:10:34,354 --> 00:10:35,646
Hi, can I help you?

69
00:10:35,813 --> 00:10:38,813
- Hi, I'm looking for Sofia Lakti.
- We are.

70
00:10:38,979 --> 00:10:40,646
- Are you family?
- Yes.

71
00:10:59,521 --> 00:11:00,896
How is she?

72
00:11:01,341 --> 00:11:02,466
In a coma

73
00:11:02,823 --> 00:11:04,063
since the accident.

74
00:11:04,346 --> 00:11:06,229
The doctors say to wait.

75
00:11:07,102 --> 00:11:09,268
- Can we see her?
- Yeah.

76
00:11:09,896 --> 00:11:11,021
Come.

77
00:12:29,896 --> 00:12:30,771
Who are you?

78
00:12:32,938 --> 00:12:33,896
Leïla,

79
00:12:34,063 --> 00:12:36,646
meet Gabriel and Driss.

80
00:12:40,979 --> 00:12:42,146
All right.

81
00:12:42,938 --> 00:12:44,729
You shouldn't be here.
Leave.

82
00:12:54,604 --> 00:12:55,688
Mom?

83
00:12:58,396 --> 00:12:59,229
Please!

84
00:13:02,521 --> 00:13:03,896
Please, Mom, no.

85
00:13:04,063 --> 00:13:06,396
Please, please, Mom.

86
00:13:08,604 --> 00:13:09,688
Fanny!

87
00:13:11,396 --> 00:13:12,979
Emergency in room 322!

88
00:13:13,396 --> 00:13:15,896
- Don't leave me.
- Miss, please.

89
00:14:11,271 --> 00:14:12,438
So?

90
00:14:18,859 --> 00:14:20,567
She died at the hospital.

91
00:14:21,604 --> 00:14:22,771
Fuck.

92
00:14:24,146 --> 00:14:26,438
- It was an accident.
- No, I was high.

93
00:14:26,938 --> 00:14:28,396
It was an accident!

94
00:14:30,063 --> 00:14:31,313
Look at me.

95
00:14:34,396 --> 00:14:35,896
It was an accident.

96
00:14:38,021 --> 00:14:41,396
- I'm a murderer.
- You were just in shock, Matthias.

97
00:14:43,563 --> 00:14:45,688
It's urgent we avoid a scandal.

98
00:14:47,896 --> 00:14:50,438
And years and years in prison.

99
00:14:53,854 --> 00:14:55,396
I'm not like you.

100
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:58,188
I'll go to the police.

101
00:14:59,396 --> 00:15:01,938
- I'll come clean.
- No, no.

102
00:15:03,744 --> 00:15:04,619
Listen!

103
00:15:05,438 --> 00:15:07,146
You act totally normal,

104
00:15:07,563 --> 00:15:09,354
but keep a low profile.

105
00:15:09,521 --> 00:15:11,229
And forget that idea.

106
00:15:11,979 --> 00:15:14,771
It's stupid to alert the police.

107
00:15:17,892 --> 00:15:19,476
Do as I say.

108
00:15:23,180 --> 00:15:24,930
Jonas will deal with it.

109
00:15:50,958 --> 00:15:53,750
- So?
- She has paperwork to finish.

110
00:15:55,250 --> 00:15:58,958
Fanny will be at the orphanage later.
She wants to talk.

111
00:15:59,139 --> 00:16:00,313
About what?

112
00:16:00,479 --> 00:16:02,063
The funeral, I think.

113
00:16:03,806 --> 00:16:05,223
Goddamn.

114
00:16:09,104 --> 00:16:11,813
I feel like an ass
for having lost touch.

115
00:16:13,354 --> 00:16:15,729
- All that lost time.
- It's life.

116
00:16:17,021 --> 00:16:17,896
No regrets?

117
00:16:18,604 --> 00:16:20,688
- That's your car?
- Yep.

118
00:16:21,813 --> 00:16:23,438
See you here at 6 pm.

119
00:16:26,729 --> 00:16:28,521
Wanna grab a drink?

120
00:16:28,813 --> 00:16:29,854
Yes.

121
00:16:30,354 --> 00:16:31,563
But alone.

122
00:17:10,729 --> 00:17:12,771
Which of them is the cop?

123
00:17:13,354 --> 00:17:16,438
They came
because they're your mom's friends.

124
00:17:16,604 --> 00:17:18,604
Local police is on the case.

125
00:17:19,521 --> 00:17:20,646
Fanny...

126
00:17:20,938 --> 00:17:23,188
No, they're not, it's been 3 days!

127
00:17:23,354 --> 00:17:25,688
We have no news.
When will we act?

128
00:17:25,854 --> 00:17:27,188
Why are you waiting?

129
00:17:27,563 --> 00:17:30,646
Why the delay?
Go away, you don't give a fuck!

130
00:17:30,813 --> 00:17:32,271
That's so not true.

131
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:44,896
Got a family?

132
00:17:47,854 --> 00:17:48,521
No.

133
00:17:50,813 --> 00:17:52,271
I had a wife.

134
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:53,271
- Driss?
- Then...

135
00:17:53,438 --> 00:17:55,104
I'm not interested.

136
00:18:02,438 --> 00:18:03,979
- It's been 20 years...
- 18.

137
00:18:04,146 --> 00:18:06,646
- Yeah, 18.
- Nothing to tell me?

138
00:18:07,854 --> 00:18:08,979
Nope.

139
00:18:15,771 --> 00:18:16,979
Great.

140
00:19:05,479 --> 00:19:06,604
Fuck it.

141
00:19:18,521 --> 00:19:21,271
CHILDREN'S HOME

142
00:19:34,021 --> 00:19:35,271
Fanny?

143
00:19:36,146 --> 00:19:37,688
I'm in the kitchen.

144
00:19:43,313 --> 00:19:44,646
There's no one?

145
00:19:45,688 --> 00:19:48,896
I sent the kids on a two-day field trip.

146
00:19:50,146 --> 00:19:53,146
I couldn't bring myself to tell them.

147
00:19:53,854 --> 00:19:55,604
They loved Sofia so much.

148
00:19:56,479 --> 00:19:59,063
Wait... Sofia worked here?

149
00:19:59,229 --> 00:20:00,271
Yeah.

150
00:20:00,563 --> 00:20:02,604
She moved back here 7 years ago.

151
00:20:03,271 --> 00:20:04,938
I needed a good counselor.

152
00:20:05,104 --> 00:20:07,563
And with her, I got the best.

153
00:20:07,729 --> 00:20:09,729
She was looking to settle down

154
00:20:09,896 --> 00:20:12,104
with her kid, someplace stable.

155
00:20:13,271 --> 00:20:17,104
In the end, Leïla grew up here
like her mother.

156
00:20:18,104 --> 00:20:19,729
You'll see...

157
00:20:19,896 --> 00:20:23,396
She's not the easiest of the lot,
but I adore her.

158
00:20:25,271 --> 00:20:26,104
Okay!

159
00:20:28,313 --> 00:20:31,146
Since the attacks
we keep our service weapons.

160
00:20:36,813 --> 00:20:38,063
I have a question.

161
00:20:38,396 --> 00:20:39,729
- Yeah?
- Where's the father?

162
00:20:42,479 --> 00:20:45,188
No husband at the hospital,
so I'm asking.

163
00:20:45,354 --> 00:20:46,271
I don't know.

164
00:20:46,938 --> 00:20:48,479
Sofia said it wasn't important.

165
00:20:50,354 --> 00:20:51,521
Still.

166
00:20:54,979 --> 00:20:56,438
Sorry, be right back.

167
00:20:59,688 --> 00:21:00,979
How about the car?

168
00:21:04,104 --> 00:21:05,479
Tell me, Fanny...

169
00:21:06,563 --> 00:21:08,271
How old is Leïla?

170
00:21:11,104 --> 00:21:12,729
She's 17.

171
00:21:14,229 --> 00:21:15,396
Thanks.

172
00:21:18,104 --> 00:21:19,938
I spoke to some colleagues.

173
00:21:20,563 --> 00:21:23,521
No leads.
They're still looking for the car.

174
00:21:25,646 --> 00:21:26,938
I'm sorry.

175
00:21:34,854 --> 00:21:36,354
Okay, come on.

176
00:21:36,521 --> 00:21:39,063
We'll bake an apple pie.

177
00:21:39,729 --> 00:21:41,646
We need something sweet.

178
00:21:46,854 --> 00:21:50,229
Damn... the mattresses
used to be way shittier!

179
00:21:51,688 --> 00:21:52,938
Special Ops?

180
00:21:57,313 --> 00:21:58,854
No... "Expendables".

181
00:22:07,438 --> 00:22:08,688
I did 5 years.

182
00:22:09,854 --> 00:22:12,604
Not my thing.
Too many charred civilians.

183
00:22:13,354 --> 00:22:18,146
I do odds and ends.
Some security work for private clients.

184
00:22:19,938 --> 00:22:22,563
Sort of... self-employed.

185
00:22:23,188 --> 00:22:24,563
Sort of legal?

186
00:22:26,104 --> 00:22:27,813
I don't take credit cards.

187
00:22:28,979 --> 00:22:29,813
I pay taxes!

188
00:22:31,438 --> 00:22:33,021
Sort of not too legal.

189
00:22:34,604 --> 00:22:35,771
Yeah.

190
00:22:39,688 --> 00:22:40,854
How about you?

191
00:22:41,604 --> 00:22:43,438
You had SWAT dreams, right?

192
00:22:45,979 --> 00:22:47,354
I made the cut.

193
00:22:50,188 --> 00:22:51,396
Good for you.

194
00:22:54,979 --> 00:22:56,063
Bravo.

195
00:23:08,563 --> 00:23:10,938
Last time
you wanted to bash my face in.

196
00:23:20,396 --> 00:23:22,021
I bashed your face in.

197
00:23:26,479 --> 00:23:28,979
- That was in a dream.
- Yeah?

198
00:23:30,229 --> 00:23:33,354
- Couldn't stand that she left?
- Who made her leave?

199
00:23:36,229 --> 00:23:38,438
She left because she was pregnant
with me.

200
00:23:40,813 --> 00:23:42,521
That's what she told me.

201
00:23:52,729 --> 00:23:55,188
- What now?
- No idea, I got no kids.

202
00:23:55,354 --> 00:23:57,521
Let's talk to her, console her.

203
00:23:57,896 --> 00:24:01,188
Give her a snuggle if you want,
I don't know how.

204
00:24:30,438 --> 00:24:31,854
<i>In a situationship?</i>

205
00:24:33,063 --> 00:24:34,063
<i>Yeah, you got it.</i>

206
00:24:34,229 --> 00:24:35,229
<i>Watch out!</i>

207
00:24:41,563 --> 00:24:42,604
<i>Sir!</i>

208
00:24:42,771 --> 00:24:44,188
<i>Sir, please!</i>

209
00:24:44,354 --> 00:24:45,854
<i>Wait!</i>

210
00:25:59,521 --> 00:26:02,771
<i>Christina Rovelli:
"My son will not take over Sécuris"</i>

211
00:26:34,521 --> 00:26:35,771
Where you going?

212
00:26:37,813 --> 00:26:38,563
Seriously?

213
00:26:39,396 --> 00:26:40,604
I won't hurt you.

214
00:26:58,229 --> 00:26:59,396
Is that all?

215
00:27:24,854 --> 00:27:25,563
Go on.

216
00:28:22,604 --> 00:28:23,771
By the way,

217
00:28:24,271 --> 00:28:25,146
Leïla.

218
00:28:28,229 --> 00:28:29,688
She's 17.

219
00:28:30,771 --> 00:28:31,813
She looks like me.

220
00:28:33,188 --> 00:28:34,771
What if I'm the father?

221
00:28:35,771 --> 00:28:36,854
What if I am?

222
00:28:39,938 --> 00:28:42,104
I'm the one Sofia loved.

223
00:28:43,146 --> 00:28:44,646
Believe what you want.

224
00:28:50,188 --> 00:28:52,271
Anyway now we'll never know.

225
00:28:53,313 --> 00:28:54,646
Honestly!

226
00:28:55,646 --> 00:28:56,813
How old are you?

227
00:28:58,646 --> 00:29:01,063
Come help me, Leïla disappeared.

228
00:29:35,771 --> 00:29:37,979
- You took my weapon?
- What?

229
00:29:38,146 --> 00:29:39,521
My gun! It was there!

230
00:29:40,104 --> 00:29:41,854
Gab, I didn't touch a thing.

231
00:29:42,771 --> 00:29:44,354
Her moped is gone.

232
00:29:45,188 --> 00:29:46,063
Oh fuck.

233
00:29:46,229 --> 00:29:49,021
How is she going to screw up this time?

234
00:29:50,646 --> 00:29:52,604
A kid won't hurt herself.

235
00:29:52,771 --> 00:29:54,688
Age isn't a factor in suicides.

236
00:29:54,854 --> 00:29:56,771
You're a teen psychologist now?

237
00:32:28,646 --> 00:32:29,646
Don't move.

238
00:32:39,604 --> 00:32:41,063
- I didn't mean to...
- Step back.

239
00:32:53,271 --> 00:32:55,104
You piece of shit.

240
00:32:55,521 --> 00:32:57,063
You didn't even call for help.

241
00:33:01,896 --> 00:33:03,521
I was scared.

242
00:33:04,146 --> 00:33:06,021
I didn't know what to do.

243
00:33:08,188 --> 00:33:10,104
I'll go to the cops.

244
00:33:10,521 --> 00:33:12,021
Forgive me.

245
00:33:12,313 --> 00:33:15,104
I think about it all night.
I can't sleep.

246
00:33:15,271 --> 00:33:17,354
Shut up, my mother's dead.

247
00:33:21,979 --> 00:33:23,354
My mother's dead

248
00:33:25,354 --> 00:33:26,771
because of you.

249
00:33:28,063 --> 00:33:29,688
I know, sorry.

250
00:33:31,063 --> 00:33:32,229
Sorry.

251
00:33:32,396 --> 00:33:33,521
Shoot, kill me.

252
00:33:34,563 --> 00:33:35,271
Go on.

253
00:33:37,771 --> 00:33:39,146
Matthias pick that up.

254
00:33:39,313 --> 00:33:40,271
Pick it up!

255
00:33:45,313 --> 00:33:47,063
What are you doing here?

256
00:33:47,479 --> 00:33:49,021
You threaten my son?

257
00:33:51,188 --> 00:33:52,188
Security!

258
00:33:53,271 --> 00:33:54,063
Wait.

259
00:33:55,604 --> 00:33:57,646
Let her go, she did nothing.

260
00:33:57,813 --> 00:33:59,938
You know we can't let her leave.

261
00:34:01,063 --> 00:34:01,896
Don't move.

262
00:34:11,063 --> 00:34:12,438
In any case,

263
00:34:14,229 --> 00:34:16,021
prison or you is the same.

264
00:34:18,563 --> 00:34:19,396
Beat it.

265
00:34:24,479 --> 00:34:25,479
Give me the gun.

266
00:34:26,688 --> 00:34:27,979
Beat it!

267
00:34:29,146 --> 00:34:30,438
Enough.

268
00:34:30,938 --> 00:34:31,938
Give it to me.

269
00:34:32,271 --> 00:34:33,146
Enough.

270
00:34:33,646 --> 00:34:35,938
- I'm fed up.
- Give it to me. Her!

271
00:34:38,688 --> 00:34:39,813
Stop!

272
00:35:22,021 --> 00:35:24,063
You know none of her friends?

273
00:35:24,229 --> 00:35:25,979
No, I mean I know them all

274
00:35:26,146 --> 00:35:27,479
but not where she is.

275
00:35:30,146 --> 00:35:31,021
It's her!

276
00:35:32,979 --> 00:35:34,104
Where are you?

277
00:35:36,354 --> 00:35:37,688
Just don't move.

278
00:35:37,854 --> 00:35:38,896
We're coming.

279
00:35:39,063 --> 00:35:40,521
Don't move.

280
00:35:41,604 --> 00:35:42,479
Train station.

281
00:35:44,813 --> 00:35:45,813
She was terrified.

282
00:36:00,146 --> 00:36:01,271
You okay?

283
00:36:02,354 --> 00:36:04,729
- Why are you wet?
- Got my gun?

284
00:36:04,896 --> 00:36:06,188
Let her breathe.

285
00:36:06,479 --> 00:36:08,063
Yeah, you're right.

286
00:36:09,396 --> 00:36:10,146
Leïla,

287
00:36:11,104 --> 00:36:12,021
breathe.

288
00:36:12,479 --> 00:36:13,729
This is important.

289
00:36:14,646 --> 00:36:17,354
- Got my gun?
- Leïla! You shoot anyone?

290
00:36:19,521 --> 00:36:21,563
- No, he...
- He shot at you?

291
00:36:22,604 --> 00:36:23,563
No, he...

292
00:36:23,729 --> 00:36:25,813
- Who he?
- The guy who killed Mom.

293
00:36:26,188 --> 00:36:27,938
- What guy?
- Matthias Rovelli.

294
00:36:28,896 --> 00:36:29,896
What happened?

295
00:36:32,396 --> 00:36:34,354
I don't know, I'm not sure.

296
00:36:34,521 --> 00:36:36,521
He got in a fight with his mother.

297
00:36:38,396 --> 00:36:40,396
He put your gun to his forehead.

298
00:36:42,146 --> 00:36:43,188
Fuck.

299
00:36:43,896 --> 00:36:45,396
There was a gunshot.

300
00:36:50,438 --> 00:36:51,104
What?

301
00:36:54,146 --> 00:36:54,938
What gunshot?

302
00:36:58,813 --> 00:37:00,063
My gun...

303
00:37:00,354 --> 00:37:01,771
is still there?

304
00:37:04,938 --> 00:37:06,396
Is it still there?

305
00:37:07,396 --> 00:37:08,729
Are you serious?

306
00:37:11,080 --> 00:37:12,080
Fuck!

307
00:37:18,271 --> 00:37:19,771
Let's get moving.

308
00:37:21,354 --> 00:37:22,521
Come.

309
00:37:29,146 --> 00:37:30,354
Keep calm.

310
00:37:31,813 --> 00:37:32,938
Calm.

311
00:37:33,729 --> 00:37:37,188
If I call the police,
there'll be an autopsy.

312
00:37:37,354 --> 00:37:38,896
Tell no one.

313
00:37:40,521 --> 00:37:42,188
You know what to do.

314
00:37:45,646 --> 00:37:48,271
I don't want to be bothered
for any reason.

315
00:37:48,896 --> 00:37:50,354
Understood, Christina.

316
00:38:07,396 --> 00:38:09,229
No way!
When did you decide

317
00:38:09,396 --> 00:38:11,479
to steal my gun to kill Rovelli?

318
00:38:11,854 --> 00:38:13,646
- Okay, lay off me.
- Sorry?

319
00:38:13,813 --> 00:38:15,146
I screwed up. I get it.

320
00:38:15,313 --> 00:38:17,354
- Stop obsessing.
- It's attempted homicide!

321
00:38:18,021 --> 00:38:19,688
You're pushing it, Leïla.

322
00:38:19,854 --> 00:38:22,896
- You too now?
- She steals my gun and mouths off.

323
00:38:23,188 --> 00:38:24,979
Kids today, what the fuck?

324
00:38:25,146 --> 00:38:26,604
Enough with your gun.

325
00:38:27,229 --> 00:38:28,354
Want a second round?

326
00:38:28,646 --> 00:38:30,896
- Let's go.
- Calm down, enough!

327
00:38:31,438 --> 00:38:33,271
Can we speak as adults?

328
00:38:34,521 --> 00:38:37,188
Leïla found the guy
who killed her mother.

329
00:38:38,146 --> 00:38:39,521
We'll go to the police

330
00:38:39,688 --> 00:38:41,188
and let them settle this.

331
00:38:41,604 --> 00:38:43,354
- We'll avoid that.
- Why?

332
00:38:43,521 --> 00:38:46,396
She'd be taken into custody
for attempted murder.

333
00:39:04,979 --> 00:39:07,229
The kid just lost her mother.

334
00:39:07,771 --> 00:39:09,229
She needs our help.

335
00:39:12,688 --> 00:39:15,438
I have an idea, but you won't like it.

336
00:39:16,229 --> 00:39:17,521
What kind of idea?

337
00:39:18,979 --> 00:39:20,813
We keep quiet for the accident.

338
00:39:21,229 --> 00:39:22,646
They keep quiet for Leïla.

339
00:39:23,521 --> 00:39:24,979
And I get my gun back.

340
00:39:25,646 --> 00:39:27,021
No, wait...

341
00:39:27,563 --> 00:39:29,479
What about Sofia in all this?

342
00:39:31,146 --> 00:39:33,188
The Rovelli kid can't just walk.

343
00:39:33,563 --> 00:39:35,354
Leïla will never stand for it.

344
00:39:35,938 --> 00:39:37,354
Nor will I.

345
00:39:44,979 --> 00:39:47,396
We get my gun and fuck them up.

346
00:39:50,063 --> 00:39:52,521
Sécuris is not a company of bouncers.

347
00:39:52,771 --> 00:39:55,604
They tried recruiting me
after Special Ops.

348
00:39:55,979 --> 00:39:58,271
Biggest security firm in Europe.

349
00:39:58,771 --> 00:39:59,979
And Rovelli?

350
00:40:00,438 --> 00:40:01,854
Brilliant woman.

351
00:40:02,021 --> 00:40:04,854
Formidable executive.
PhD in Military Ops.

352
00:40:05,021 --> 00:40:07,813
Specialist in warfare, lawfare, etc.

353
00:40:08,396 --> 00:40:10,854
Eminence grise
known the world over.

354
00:40:11,021 --> 00:40:12,938
With quite the contact list.

355
00:40:13,104 --> 00:40:16,313
Yeah, I see.
Every reason to avoid a scandal.

356
00:40:16,688 --> 00:40:17,813
Exactly.

357
00:40:21,604 --> 00:40:23,521
Leïla's got guts.

358
00:40:26,146 --> 00:40:27,354
You know,

359
00:40:28,021 --> 00:40:30,771
stealing a cop's gun
to avenge her mom...

360
00:40:31,021 --> 00:40:35,104
Well, the cop is me
and it's totally reckless.

361
00:40:37,646 --> 00:40:39,604
I think she takes after me.

362
00:40:40,271 --> 00:40:42,646
Starting your career as a dad?

363
00:40:43,271 --> 00:40:45,813
You don't care who Leïla's father is?

364
00:40:46,938 --> 00:40:48,104
It matters.

365
00:40:48,271 --> 00:40:50,688
What matters
is solving this clusterfuck.

366
00:40:51,146 --> 00:40:53,063
We'll work out the family later.

367
00:40:53,979 --> 00:40:55,938
See? We are a family.

368
00:40:56,104 --> 00:40:57,521
No... shut up.

369
00:40:57,688 --> 00:40:59,521
- You said family.
- I said shut up.

370
00:41:03,188 --> 00:41:04,771
He said family.

371
00:41:06,979 --> 00:41:08,354
You sure of this plan?

372
00:41:09,521 --> 00:41:10,813
It's your plan.

373
00:41:12,313 --> 00:41:13,438
Exactly.

374
00:41:28,479 --> 00:41:29,521
Police.

375
00:41:30,271 --> 00:41:31,521
That sucked.

376
00:41:38,146 --> 00:41:40,563
<i>Search by serial number</i>

377
00:41:55,563 --> 00:41:56,479
Your ID?

378
00:42:05,146 --> 00:42:06,521
He's the witness.

379
00:42:07,146 --> 00:42:08,229
Good evening.

380
00:42:15,146 --> 00:42:16,188
Evening.

381
00:42:19,188 --> 00:42:20,354
How can we help you?

382
00:42:21,438 --> 00:42:23,521
This man was walking his dog

383
00:42:23,688 --> 00:42:25,938
and heard a gunshot in this house.

384
00:42:26,104 --> 00:42:27,271
A gunshot?

385
00:42:27,854 --> 00:42:30,146
There were no gunshots here, sir.

386
00:42:30,604 --> 00:42:33,646
This is the Rovelli residence.
Madam is seeing no one.

387
00:42:33,813 --> 00:42:37,021
Perfect.
We came to see Matthias Rovelli.

388
00:42:39,354 --> 00:42:40,604
Is he here?

389
00:42:42,021 --> 00:42:43,354
Not that I'm aware of.

390
00:42:45,104 --> 00:42:46,604
You must leave us now.

391
00:42:49,729 --> 00:42:52,854
Three days ago Matthias Rovelli
killed someone.

392
00:42:53,021 --> 00:42:54,521
A hit and run.

393
00:42:55,313 --> 00:42:56,729
Can we talk?

394
00:42:59,854 --> 00:43:01,146
Wait here.

395
00:43:24,063 --> 00:43:25,146
Madame Rovelli.

396
00:43:30,813 --> 00:43:32,021
Matthias isn't in?

397
00:43:34,688 --> 00:43:36,396
What do you want from him?

398
00:43:36,688 --> 00:43:38,146
Just to talk.

399
00:43:38,688 --> 00:43:40,063
A girl came here earlier.

400
00:43:40,688 --> 00:43:41,688
With a gun.

401
00:43:51,938 --> 00:43:53,021
Follow me.

402
00:44:13,229 --> 00:44:14,146
An orphan...

403
00:44:16,521 --> 00:44:18,979
is what we become
when we lose a parent.

404
00:44:22,604 --> 00:44:25,188
But for a mother who loses her son

405
00:44:25,771 --> 00:44:26,979
there is no word.

406
00:44:31,729 --> 00:44:32,438
Jonas.

407
00:44:34,854 --> 00:44:36,313
Sig-Sauer.

408
00:44:36,479 --> 00:44:38,229
SP 2022. Serial number:

409
00:44:38,396 --> 00:44:41,646
S-073-1-2-5,

410
00:44:42,188 --> 00:44:44,563
belonging to Commander Gabriel Stenne,

411
00:44:44,896 --> 00:44:46,813
Internal Affairs.

412
00:44:47,521 --> 00:44:50,396
- Internal Affairs?
- Not now.

413
00:44:50,729 --> 00:44:52,563
Leïla Lakti used your gun

414
00:44:52,729 --> 00:44:54,563
to cause Matthias' death.

415
00:44:59,771 --> 00:45:01,729
First we'll deal with you.

416
00:45:02,521 --> 00:45:04,979
Then we'll pay a visit to Leïla.

417
00:45:06,771 --> 00:45:08,813
With all due respect, Mrs. Rovelli,

418
00:45:10,354 --> 00:45:12,271
no one touches my daughter.

419
00:45:14,813 --> 00:45:15,979
- Excuse me?
- What?

420
00:45:16,521 --> 00:45:18,438
- What was that?
- What was what?

421
00:45:18,604 --> 00:45:21,063
- Now she's your kid?
- Now you want one?

422
00:45:21,229 --> 00:45:22,771
This has to be settled.

423
00:45:22,938 --> 00:45:24,896
- Let's settle it now.
- Let's.

424
00:45:25,271 --> 00:45:26,813
- Round 2?
- You bet.

425
00:45:26,979 --> 00:45:27,729
Enough.

426
00:45:28,604 --> 00:45:29,354
Shit!

427
00:45:32,604 --> 00:45:35,146
Let's take it easy, okay?

428
00:45:40,729 --> 00:45:41,938
Lower your gun.

429
00:45:42,438 --> 00:45:43,771
Lower it.

430
00:45:50,146 --> 00:45:51,354
Kick it away.

431
00:45:55,313 --> 00:45:56,938
This is what you want?

432
00:45:58,646 --> 00:45:59,813
Yeah.

433
00:46:03,854 --> 00:46:04,813
Take it.

434
00:46:07,354 --> 00:46:08,021
And leave.

435
00:46:28,938 --> 00:46:29,688
Stop!

436
00:46:34,063 --> 00:46:34,938
Let them leave.

437
00:47:00,813 --> 00:47:04,188
- We need them dead.
- Recruit a team, not solo.

438
00:47:12,729 --> 00:47:14,104
What do we do?

439
00:47:14,563 --> 00:47:15,438
Fanny, it's me.

440
00:47:16,354 --> 00:47:17,896
Is there still the cabin?

441
00:47:19,396 --> 00:47:21,604
Take Leïla and wait for us there.

442
00:47:22,646 --> 00:47:24,604
Please, do as I say, Fanny.

443
00:47:27,771 --> 00:47:29,521
All of us in a safe place.

444
00:47:30,188 --> 00:47:31,438
Then what?

445
00:47:32,979 --> 00:47:34,104
Then we'll see.

446
00:48:04,771 --> 00:48:06,146
Some serious shit.

447
00:48:07,229 --> 00:48:08,604
That's basically it.

448
00:48:25,729 --> 00:48:27,979
Can we have an explanation now?

449
00:48:35,729 --> 00:48:37,021
Matthias Rovelli is dead.

450
00:48:39,521 --> 00:48:40,396
What?

451
00:48:40,938 --> 00:48:43,771
And his mother,
who happens to be a psycho,

452
00:48:43,938 --> 00:48:46,063
thinks that Leïla killed him.

453
00:48:51,438 --> 00:48:52,396
Look at me.

454
00:48:53,021 --> 00:48:54,354
Look at me.

455
00:48:54,688 --> 00:48:57,021
I saw the wound, there's no doubt.

456
00:48:57,188 --> 00:48:58,479
It was a suicide.

457
00:48:59,396 --> 00:49:00,438
Yeah, but...

458
00:49:00,729 --> 00:49:02,646
Leïla can't stay in Biarritz.

459
00:49:03,063 --> 00:49:04,688
What are they after?

460
00:49:07,313 --> 00:49:08,563
They want me dead?

461
00:49:13,271 --> 00:49:14,396
She has the means.

462
00:49:16,354 --> 00:49:18,146
I'll have a word with her.

463
00:49:18,313 --> 00:49:20,063
- No, Fanny, bad idea.
- Why?

464
00:49:20,229 --> 00:49:22,813
She's dangerous.
We leave early tomorrow.

465
00:49:22,979 --> 00:49:23,813
Listen,

466
00:49:23,979 --> 00:49:25,896
my pals can protect Leïla.

467
00:49:26,063 --> 00:49:27,313
Spare us your pals.

468
00:49:27,479 --> 00:49:29,104
Better than your cop buds.

469
00:49:30,688 --> 00:49:32,313
Quick word outside?

470
00:49:37,729 --> 00:49:38,646
Be right back.

471
00:49:47,938 --> 00:49:49,688
What did you do, Leïla?

472
00:49:50,896 --> 00:49:52,479
What did you do?

473
00:49:53,229 --> 00:49:55,896
What's your problem?
Be happy you got your gun.

474
00:49:56,063 --> 00:49:57,813
Yes, and now that I have it,

475
00:49:58,313 --> 00:50:00,063
it's time to call my colleagues.

476
00:50:00,229 --> 00:50:01,354
You don't get it.

477
00:50:01,938 --> 00:50:03,563
She controls this region.

478
00:50:03,979 --> 00:50:05,813
So I'll call <i>my</i> colleagues.

479
00:50:17,104 --> 00:50:20,063
Can Sécuris track our cell phones?

480
00:50:38,688 --> 00:50:39,729
Fanny!

481
00:50:39,896 --> 00:50:41,396
Your phone, please.

482
00:50:44,063 --> 00:50:45,188
Thanks.

483
00:50:46,313 --> 00:50:47,479
Your phone.

484
00:50:48,229 --> 00:50:50,021
- Dream on.
- Sorry.

485
00:50:52,104 --> 00:50:53,063
He's a lunatic.

486
00:50:55,688 --> 00:50:56,729
Give that back.

487
00:50:57,396 --> 00:50:58,563
Fuck!

488
00:50:59,396 --> 00:51:01,521
Why throw away my phone?

489
00:51:01,688 --> 00:51:04,229
No choice. Safety reasons.

490
00:51:05,563 --> 00:51:07,438
You're such fucking pains!

491
00:51:11,979 --> 00:51:13,063
What?

492
00:51:15,271 --> 00:51:16,354
What?

493
00:51:28,188 --> 00:51:29,729
Look what I found.

494
00:51:32,396 --> 00:51:34,146
It waited 18 years for us.

495
00:51:48,354 --> 00:51:51,896
She told her dad,
so I got discharged from SWAT.

496
00:51:53,563 --> 00:51:56,021
Yeah, keep on laughing, son of a bitch!

497
00:51:56,313 --> 00:51:57,646
Goddamn!

498
00:51:58,271 --> 00:52:00,896
Mine shot at me. With my gun.

499
00:52:01,063 --> 00:52:03,479
You know what? I understand her.

500
00:52:06,438 --> 00:52:10,313
When the cops came,
I was naked and gushing blood,

501
00:52:10,479 --> 00:52:11,896
with a dislocated shoulder:

502
00:52:12,063 --> 00:52:15,146
"It's all good, sir,
a little construction work."

503
00:52:18,396 --> 00:52:20,104
Women aren't our strong point.

504
00:52:27,771 --> 00:52:29,021
I only loved Sofia.

505
00:52:30,979 --> 00:52:32,271
You too?

506
00:52:44,063 --> 00:52:47,104
- Was it you or her who...
- Driss...

507
00:52:50,021 --> 00:52:51,854
- What?
- Fucking traitor.

508
00:53:07,521 --> 00:53:08,729
What?

509
00:53:09,313 --> 00:53:11,521
Don't act like a cop.

510
00:53:17,771 --> 00:53:18,854
What do you do?

511
00:53:21,271 --> 00:53:22,854
Not even he knows.

512
00:53:32,313 --> 00:53:33,646
How did your parents die?

513
00:53:36,396 --> 00:53:38,063
House caught on fire.

514
00:53:38,438 --> 00:53:40,146
I was sleeping at a friend's.

515
00:53:40,854 --> 00:53:43,521
My mom killed herself,
never met my dad.

516
00:53:47,979 --> 00:53:49,229
Cool.

517
00:53:54,271 --> 00:53:56,271
What was the deal with Mom?

518
00:53:56,938 --> 00:53:59,646
- We all grew up together.
- At the Home.

519
00:54:00,229 --> 00:54:01,646
Bonds form.

520
00:54:04,229 --> 00:54:06,146
We were both in love with her.

521
00:54:06,604 --> 00:54:08,396
That created fewer bonds.

522
00:54:09,188 --> 00:54:11,188
You mean, you went out with her?

523
00:54:12,854 --> 00:54:14,813
- Yep.
- Not at the same time.

524
00:54:15,771 --> 00:54:16,854
Close enough.

525
00:54:18,729 --> 00:54:21,021
So one of you is
my biological dad.

526
00:54:33,771 --> 00:54:35,896
I look more like Driss though.

527
00:54:36,479 --> 00:54:37,604
That means nothing.

528
00:54:41,896 --> 00:54:44,354
You sure do look a lot like your mom.

529
00:54:52,104 --> 00:54:53,438
I'm scared.

530
00:55:01,313 --> 00:55:02,896
Now you should reassure me.

531
00:55:04,646 --> 00:55:05,729
It'll all be fine.

532
00:55:10,688 --> 00:55:12,688
Jeez, are you two pathetic!

533
00:55:14,854 --> 00:55:15,813
Really lame.

534
00:55:45,563 --> 00:55:46,979
Not very legal.

535
00:55:49,563 --> 00:55:51,021
Yeah, who cares?

536
00:55:56,104 --> 00:55:57,396
Give the kids a kiss.

537
00:55:57,813 --> 00:55:59,146
Time to go.

538
00:56:07,938 --> 00:56:09,563
You got girlfriends?

539
00:56:13,688 --> 00:56:14,896
No comment.

540
00:56:15,063 --> 00:56:16,188
Ditto.

541
00:56:17,563 --> 00:56:18,854
A guy?

542
00:56:20,104 --> 00:56:21,313
Maybe.

543
00:56:33,771 --> 00:56:35,438
We better switch cars.

544
00:56:43,063 --> 00:56:44,021
Got him.

545
00:56:44,729 --> 00:56:45,563
Go right.

546
00:56:53,979 --> 00:56:55,563
Problem with my car?

547
00:56:55,729 --> 00:56:57,229
I'd prefer low-key.

548
00:56:58,063 --> 00:57:01,646
- Is your face low-key?
- I get stopped less than you.

549
00:57:02,104 --> 00:57:05,521
I get stopped because they're jealous.
Of my car.

550
00:57:06,146 --> 00:57:07,813
Not of your shirt?

551
00:57:09,229 --> 00:57:11,271
What does Mulan want?

552
00:57:27,813 --> 00:57:29,854
Remember the gypsies
who chased us?

553
00:57:30,021 --> 00:57:31,771
No, it was the crime squad.

554
00:57:32,104 --> 00:57:33,146
Same difference.

555
00:57:33,313 --> 00:57:34,188
Guys!

556
00:57:37,438 --> 00:57:38,354
Floor it!

557
00:57:49,021 --> 00:57:50,104
Move!

558
00:57:52,271 --> 00:57:53,021
Drop it!

559
00:57:54,646 --> 00:57:55,563
Don't look!

560
00:57:56,229 --> 00:57:56,896
Get out!

561
00:58:15,729 --> 00:58:18,271
- <i>So?</i>
- All good. We have the girl.

562
00:58:22,938 --> 00:58:23,938
Take the car.

